lib/libhybris-common.so.1, lib/libhardware.so.2, lib/libhybris-vulkan-icd.so.0, lib/libhybris/linker/q.so
  libhybris, https://github.com/taowen/libhybris (arlinux branch; the commit is in SOURCES), with
  mali-g2/hybris/patches applied. libhybris-common, libhardware and the Vulkan ICD are under the
  Apache License 2.0 (Apache-2.0); the linker (q.so) is derived from Android's bionic linker and is
  under the BSD 2-Clause license (BSD-2-Clause), with parts under the Apache License 2.0.
  Built against Halium's android-headers (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/Halium/android-headers.
  Some of the code compiled into them is under other permissive licences, reproduced below:
  strlcpy.c and strlcat.c (ISC; in libhybris-common.so.1 and q.so), integrity_sha256.c (MIT, from
  BearSSL; in q.so) and bionic's private/bionic_asm_arm64.h (BSD-3-Clause; in q.so).
  q.so also contains GCC's libsupc++, under the GCC Runtime Library Exception.

At run time these libraries load the device's own Android system libraries and Vulkan driver from
/system, /vendor and /apex; none of them is distributed here.


